
# Commit Message Template
#
# Always use Angular Conventional Commits specification (MUST FOLLOW EXACTLY).
#
# Single-line format:
# <type>(<scope>): <description>
#
# Multiline format:
# <type>(<scope>): <description>
# - <description_line_1>.
# - <description_line_2>.
# - ...
#
# Field Definitions:
# - <type>: One of "build", "ci", "docs", "feat", "fix", "perf", "refactor", "revert", "style", or "test"
# - <scope>: Optional area affected (e.g. zsh, make, brew, git)
# - <description>: Generated commit message describing the changes
# - <description_line_X>: Message for a different concern in multiline format
# - <summary>: Short summary of changes for post-review fixes
#
# Types:
# - build: Changes to the build system or external dependencies
# - ci: Changes to CI configuration files and scripts
# - docs: Documentation changes
# - feat: A new feature
# - fix: A bug fix
# - perf: Code change that improves performance
# - refactor: Code change that neither fixes a bug nor adds a feature
# - revert: Reverts a previous commit
# - style: Formatting, missing semi-colons, etc.
# - test: Adding missing tests or correcting existing tests
#
# Format Rules:
# - Use the imperative, present tense ("change", not "changed")
# - Do not capitalize the first letter of the summary
# - No dot (.) at the end of the summary
# - Each bullet point MUST start with - (dash and space)
# - NEVER add a "Generated with Claude" disclaimer, author info, or other extra content
# - Post-review commits: Use multiline format with first bullet starting "<summary>"
#
# Examples:
# feat(zsh): add user authentication
# perf(zsh): reduce shell startup time
# docs: update documentation for API endpoints
#
# Multiline example:
# feat: implement dashboard analytics
# - Add user activity tracking components
# - Create data visualization charts
# - Integrate with reporting API
#
# Post-review fixes example:
# fix(data): memory leak in data processor
# - Buffer management optimization
# - Update error handling for edge cases
# - Add missing null checks
